        "id": "s9",
        "kind": "summary",
        "title": "Summary",
        "body": "- $\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}$; there is no rule for adding roots.\n- Simplify with the largest square factor: $\\sqrt{48} = 4\\sqrt{3}$.\n- Like surds add: $2\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} = 5\\sqrt{2}$.\n- Expand brackets with FOIL; $\\sqrt{3}\\times\\sqrt{3} = 3$.\n- Rationalise by multiplying by the surd, or by the conjugate when the denominator has two terms.",
        "visuals": [
