      "gradeBand": "8-9",
      "skill": "show-that with surds",
      "calculator": "non-calculator",
      "tags": [],
      "solution": "Route 1: $(3+\\sqrt{2})^2 = 9 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 2 = 11 + 6\\sqrt{2}$ and $(3-\\sqrt{2})^2 = 11 - 6\\sqrt{2}$; subtracting gives $12\\sqrt{2}$. Route 2: $a^2 - b^2 = (a+b)(a-b) = 6 \\times 2\\sqrt{2} = 12\\sqrt{2}$. Either route scores full marks if every step is on the page.",
