        {
          "code": "M1",
          "marks": 1,
          "description": "One bracket squared correctly"
        },
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "marks": 1,
          "description": "Both squared, or difference of two squares used"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "marks": 1,
          "description": "$12\\sqrt{2}$ reached with working"
        }
      ],
      "discriminators": [
        "show-that"
      ],
      "suggestedMinutes": 4,
      "criteria": [
        {
          "text": "A correct route started: both brackets expanded with the middle terms shown, or the difference of two squares $(a+b)(a-b)$ set up",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Correct intermediate values: $11 \\pm 6\\sqrt{2}$, or $(a+b) = 6$ and $(a-b) = 2\\sqrt{2}$",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "$12\\sqrt{2}$ reached with every step written",
          "marks": 1
        }
      ],
      "modelAnswer": "$(3+\\sqrt{2})^2 = 9 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 2 = 11 + 6\\sqrt{2}$. $(3-\\sqrt{2})^2 = 9 - 6\\sqrt{2} + 2 = 11 - 6\\sqrt{2}$. Subtracting: $(11 + 6\\sqrt{2}) - (11 - 6\\sqrt{2}) = 12\\sqrt{2}$, as required."
