      "Adding roots: writing $\\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{16} = \\sqrt{25}$.",
      "Stopping at $2\\sqrt{12}$ instead of going on to $4\\sqrt{3}$.",
      "Squaring a bracket term by term: $(\\sqrt{5}+1)^2 = 5 + 1$.",
      "Multiplying by the surd instead of the conjugate when the denominator has two terms.",
      "Giving a decimal from a calculator on Paper 1."
    ],
    "grade9Looks": "A grade 9 answer spots the largest square factor first time, keeps every value exact, uses the conjugate without being told, and in show-that questions writes the middle terms of every expansion before collecting."
